<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander II of Imereti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1510</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a> was king of Imereti in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1484 to 1510, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrat-vi-of-georgia">Bagrat II of Imereti</a>. He held the kingdom against rivals and was recognised as overlord by the princes of Mingrelia, Guria and Abkhazia, though his attempts to take Kartli failed. In the last year of his reign the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> raided Imereti for the first time and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutaisi">Kutaisi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-imereti.jpg" alt="Alexander II of Imereti" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This image has been extracted from another file · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_II_of_Imereti_(crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
